<!--
  RSW_DragonsnakeAlbino.xml — DRAGONSNAKE_PAIR_BUILD_ONE_PALE_ONE_PROPER (2026-10-17)

  Owner, 2026-10-17 (canon blog-image review sheet, verbatim): "Split into two official versions. The two pale
  versions let's call Dragonsnake_albino. The Jedi Fallen Order four variants lets accept as the canon Dragonsnake.
  Comission both in our Star Wars fauna mod."
  Spec: design/RimStarWars/canon_references/dragonsnake_albino/description.md (`## Must show` is the bar):
  a gigantic pale bone-white LIMBLESS serpent, long narrow skull-like head with no visible eyes, many long needle
  fangs dripping venom, glossy ringed coils (The Mandalorian and Grogu — the Hutt Twins' pit beast, whose venom
  injured Din Djarin).

  WHERE IT LIVES (design call, recorded in Transient/afk_2026-10-17/dragonsnake_build.md): a RARE pale variant in
  exactly the swamps its canon parent RSW_Dragonsnake already holds — no new biome, no roster eviction. Canon gives
  it no separate habitat (it is a dragonsnake of Nal Hutta's swamps, kept captive by the Hutts), so it follows the
  parent: race.wildBiomes below mirror the parent's vanilla swamp rows at one sixth, and its Greentide rows
  (RUT_Greentide + RM_Greentide, 0.02 against the parent's 0.12) are patch-added by
  RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_Greentide.xml, guarded on this def existing.

  Body: its own limbless BodyDef below (the serpent plan the donor's dragonsnake body had, minus the hood the film
  creature lacks); the canon Dragonsnake's body is now a quadruped. Eyes stay as parts, relabelled "vestigial eye
  pit": canon shows no visible eyes, and an eyeless body would read as blind in the game's sight capacity.

  Breeding: it lays the dragonsnake's own eggs, which hatch ordinary dragonsnakes (CompHatcher names one pawn kind) —
  read in game as albinism being recessive: a pale parent does not breed true, so the albino stays rare.

  Venom: its bite is vanilla ToxicBite (canon: its venom felled Din Djarin). Sounds reuse the dragonsnake's.

  Mod Settings: "Albino dragonsnake" (RSW_BeastMechanicsSettings.albinoDragonsnakeEnabled, default on). Off, the
  startup pass RSW_DragonsnakeAlbinoToggle removes it from every biome roster; nothing else changes.

  Art: texPaths below are RimStarWars/SWBestiary/DragonsnakeAlbino/*. Until art.py installs them this file is held by
  src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt (pink squares otherwise). Candidate already rendered: artpipe regen_gt_canon_dragonsnake_v1
  (the pale serpent currently installed on RSW_Dragonsnake's own path).
-->
